{
  "about": "Every job a model can be hired for, and the public signals that decide who gets it. w = weight. higher=false means lower is better (latency, price, error rate). log=true scales the value logarithmically first (prices, context sizes, time horizons). A metric no source reported this week is left out of that week's weighting. Metric prefixes: Public sources: arena = Arena dataset, llmstats = llm-stats.com, epoch = Epoch AI's own data, x = derived (price, context). Personal-build sources (opt-in, never published): aa = Artificial Analysis API, epochx = third-party results re-hosted by Epoch, benchlm, eqbench. 'essential' lists signals a job can't be ranked without.",
